# The QML modules the 355 QML checks of lockscreen/, sddm/, signin/ and
# session/polkit load. They happen to arrive with plasma-workspace today,
# and a test that depends on another package's dependency list is a test
# that breaks the day that list is tidied.
# python3-pil and python3-numpy are <!nocheck>, and the build could not
# be made without them. debian/rules broadened its test step to `pytest
# tests/ grub/tests/ art/` on 2026-11-06 08:24 (61cad14, "the package build
# named its test folders, and missed 346 tests") -- a correct change, and the
# first one to put art/ inside the gate that decides whether the ISO ships.
#
# art/signin.py imports PIL at module level, so without it pytest dies
# COLLECTING art/test_signin.py:
#     ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'PIL'
#     Interrupted: 1 error during collection
# and an interrupted collection runs nothing: 0 of art/'s 326 checks, not 13.
# Measured 2026-11-07 -- it is what stopped the image build, 36 minutes in.
#
# numpy is the same gate, quieter: art/test_sounds.py does
# `pytest.importorskip("numpy")` at module level, so without it those 12
# checks SKIP instead of failing -- and they are real assertions about the
# waveforms (finite samples, peak under 1.0, DC offset, fade-out). Twelve
# tests silently absent from the release gate is exactly what 61cad14 was
# written to stop, so adding PIL alone would have left the job half done.
               python3-numpy <!nocheck>,
               python3-pil <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtmultimedia <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qttest <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-controls <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-effects <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-shapes <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-templates <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-virtualkeyboard <!nocheck>,
               qml6-module-qtquick-window <!nocheck>,
               qt6-base-dev,
               qt6-declarative-dev,
               qt6-declarative-dev-tools,
               qt6-svg-dev,
# qt6-svg-dev does not bring the SVG image plugin, and without it
# art/icons/test_render.py cannot draw a single icon
               qt6-svg-plugins <!nocheck>
